<title>UK: Legal &amp; General H1 profit, dividend higher.</title>
<headline>Legal &amp; General H1 profit, dividend higher.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ending June 30</p>
<p>				   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		18.02		  vs 17.10</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 8.75		   vs 7.70</p>
<p> Operating profit	 134.3		  vs 111.1</p>
<p> Life and pensions	123.4		  vs 87.0</p>
<p> Pretax		     1,508.8		vs 119.1</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts' forecasts on pre-tax profits were in a range of 119 to 136 million stg. The pretax profit figure for this year includes 1.402 billion stg relating to the reclassification of shareholders' retained capital.  </p>
<p> Tax			  31.6		   vs 35.1</p>
<p> Net taxed		  1,477.2		vs 84.0</p>
<p> Investment income	26.5		   vs 25.8</p>
<p> Interest payable	 6.0		    vs 5.3</p>
<p> Retained		   1,433.8		vs 46.0</p>
<p> Pay date		   December 2</p>
<p>Div registration date  October 1</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
